"epic overview" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		&lt;epic-overview&gt;
		<header>The &lt;epic-overview&gt; element: an epic page's first section, 1. Overview.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph><text code>&lt;epic-overview&gt;</> is an epic page's first section, "1. Overview".</>
	<list bulleted>
		<item>It holds the two-sentence summary, the prompt that started the plan, and the Overview's numbered sub-sections.</>
		<item>It draws the title bar with its lightbulb, the fold, and the estimate line.</>
	</>

	<!-- no ui-list.spell-meta here:  any ui-item element on the page leaves epic-item unstyled (issue I9 of epic-components) -->
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Written for: anyone reading or writing an epic page's markup, or changing this element.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Status: <label size="mini" color="green">built</> in <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-overview" link="/epic/src/components/epic-overview/"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-overview/" code>epic-overview/</></>.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its vocabulary (attributes, slots, parts, children): <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-overview-epicoverview-en-ts" link="/epic/src/components/epic-overview/EpicOverview.en.ts"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-overview/EpicOverview.en.ts" code>EpicOverview.en.ts</></>.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>The component: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-overview-epicoverview-tsx" link="/epic/src/components/epic-overview/EpicOverview.tsx"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-overview/EpicOverview.tsx" code>EpicOverview.tsx</></>.</>

	<section label="1. Example">
		<icon slot="icon" name="eye"/>
		<example "Example">
			<html>
				<epic-overview id="overview" estimate="44h-56h in all, 3h left">
					<epic-summary>Plan docs drawn by Solid web components (<code>&lt;epic-page&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;epic-item&gt;</code> ...) in a new package, <a href="/spell-epic/" target="src-spell-epic" title="spell-epic"><code>epics</code></a>, loaded by <code>&lt;ui-root&gt;</code> as a component pack, so a doc holds only its data and prose.</epic-summary>
					<epic-prompt>
						<p>Plan docs (epic pages) as Solid web components, instead of HTML that carries its own layout.</p>
					</epic-prompt>
					<epic-section id="o1" kind="overview-part" title="Structure">
						<p>A new package, <a href="/spell-epic/" target="src-spell-epic" title="spell-epic"><code>epics</code></a>, holds the plan doc's elements and the one description of each.</p>
					</epic-section>
					<epic-section id="o2" kind="overview-part" title="A doc, before and after">
						<p>The same doc, in the old markup and in the new.</p>
					</epic-section>
				</epic-overview>
			</html>
		</example>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Click its title to open it: the summary (a lede), the folded Kickoff prompt, the estimate line, then the sub-sections <text code>1.1 Structure</> and <text code>1.2 A doc, before and after</>, each folding on its own.</>
			<item>⌥-click (Alt-click) on its chevron or title opens it and everything in it at once: its sub-sections, their items and asides, parts loading as they open. On an open Overview it folds everything inside, then the Overview itself.</>
			<item>Its number is its place among the page's blocks: always <text code>1</>.</>
			<item>Taken from <link target="epic-components" link="/epics/epic-components/epic-components.plan.html#overview">this epic's own Overview</>, cut short.</>
		</>

		<section label="With buttons in its title row" sticky collapsible dividing open="false">
			<text paragraph>A page's own buttons go in its title row: <text code>&lt;ui-button slot="actions"&gt;</> children (epic <text code>epic-workflow</> P25).</>
			<list bulleted>
				<item>They sit after the title, before its review buttons (while the page is reviewed); the fold chevron is at the row's start.</>
				<item>A click on one never folds or unfolds it.</>
				<item>The docs runtime puts the Overview's bullhorn there too, first: a comment on the whole Overview. Its summary and prose keep their own bullhorns, over their corners.</>
			</>
			<example "With buttons in its title row">
				<html>
					<epic-overview id="overview-example">
						<epic-summary>Every folding element's title row takes the page's own buttons.</epic-summary>
						<ui-button slot="actions" appearance="circular basic" size="mini" icon="copy" title="Copy a link to it" aria-label="Copy a link to it"></ui-button>
					</epic-overview>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="While the page is reviewed" sticky collapsible dividing open="false">
			<text paragraph>On a reviewed epic page, the Overview takes review notes on its title row, as an item does on its line (epic <text code>epic-engine</> I55;  2026-10-20: "The buttons on the left should move into the 1. Overview header, as well as a bullhorn").</>
			<list bulleted>
				<item>In its title row, in order: the bullhorn, then Make Todo and Revisit in one pill; the fold chevron at the row's start.</>
				<item>While the page agrees its Overview (<text code>stage="overview"</>), <text bold>Accept Overview</> comes last in the row, a green thumbs up and its words (<text code>&lt;epic-stage-button&gt;</>, epic <text code>epic-engine</> I180;  in the header's Send before):  it's there while the Overview is folded. A press starts a five-minute countdown, a green ring round the thumbs up (I181):  a second press calls it off;  run out, it accepts the Overview and sends.  Outlined green until the session moves the page on.</>
				<item>Revisit opens it and its note box, right under the title row, above the summary. Leaving the box empty closes it.</>
				<item>A marked note shows there too, with its Edit.</>
				<item>The marks are keyed <text code>summary</> in the review inbox, as the summary's were: only an Overview holding an <text code>&lt;epic-summary&gt;</> takes them.</>
				<item>Before, <text code>&lt;epic-summary&gt;</> drew the buttons and an open note box under its lede.</>
				<item>They need the page server and a page's review inbox, so this page can't show them: <link target="src-guides-epic-components-review-html" link="/guides/epic-components/review.html">Reviewing an Epic Page</> shows them on a real epic page.</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Markup">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<text paragraph>From a real epic page (<link title="epics/solid-migration/solid-migration.plan.html" target="solid-migration" link="/epics/solid-migration/solid-migration.plan.html"><text code>solid-migration.plan.html</></>), the summary cut short:</>
		<text paragraph>An Overview:</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<epic-overview id="overview">
			  <epic-summary>... two sentences ...</epic-summary>
			  <epic-prompt><p>convert this into a plan doc with name "solid-migration"</p></epic-prompt>
			  <epic-section id="o1" kind="overview-part" title="Where it stands" source="parts/o1.html"></epic-section>
			  <epic-section id="o2" kind="overview-part" title="Design" source="parts/o2.html"></epic-section>
			  <epic-section id="o3" kind="overview-part" title="Path map" source="parts/o3.html"></epic-section>
			</epic-overview>
			```
		</>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Its <text code>id</> is always <text code>overview</>.</>
			<item>Each sub-section's body is usually in a PART FILE (<text code>source="parts/o1.html"</>): a file of its own, loaded the first time it opens.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Where it goes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="compass"/>

		<section label="Its parents" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>Parent</>
					<cell>How</>
					<cell>How many</>
					<cell>As</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-page-html" link="/epic-page">
							<text code>&lt;epic-page&gt;</>
						</>
					</>
					<cell/>
					<cell>exactly one</>
					<cell>1. Overview.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Its children" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<text paragraph>The summary, the prompt, then the sub-sections. Older docs held the summary and the prompt in slots (<text code>&lt;p slot="summary"&gt;</>, <text code>&lt;blockquote slot="prompt"&gt;</>); they still draw in the same places.</>
			<text paragraph>In THIS order, always: the tool puts each child where it belongs, and the check refuses another order.</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>Child</>
					<cell>Where</>
					<cell>How many</>
					<cell>What it is</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>prose</>
					<cell>
						<text code>slot="summary"</>
					</>
					<cell>one at most</>
					<cell>The summary, in older docs.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>prose</>
					<cell>
						<text code>slot="prompt"</>
					</>
					<cell>one at most</>
					<cell>The kickoff prompt, in older docs.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-summary-html" link="/epic-summary">
							<text code>&lt;epic-summary&gt;</>
						</>
					</>
					<cell/>
					<cell>one at most</>
					<cell>The summary, two sentences.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-prompt-html" link="/epic-prompt">
							<text code>&lt;epic-prompt&gt;</>
						</>
					</>
					<cell/>
					<cell>one at most</>
					<cell>The kickoff prompt, as typed.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>prose</>
					<cell/>
					<cell>any number</>
					<cell>Prose before the sub-sections (older docs).</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-section-html" link="/epic-section">
							<text code>&lt;epic-section kind="overview-part"&gt;</>
						</>
					</>
					<cell/>
					<cell>any number</>
					<cell>The sub-sections, <text code>o1</>, <text code>o2</> ...</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="4. Attributes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="table columns"/>
		<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
			<row header>
				<cell>Name</>
				<cell>Values</>
				<cell>Meaning</>
				<cell>Required</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>id</>
					<space/>
					<text class="meta">JS property: <text code>epicId</></>
				</>
				<cell>
					<text code>overview</>
				</>
				<cell>Always <text code>overview</>: links land on it (<text code>#overview</>).</>
				<cell>yes</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>estimate</>
				</>
				<cell>text</>
				<cell>The total estimate, as the script adds it up from the phases (<text code>4h-5h 30m in all, 2h-3h left (P5 not estimated)</>). Absent before the first phase.</>
				<cell/>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>open</>
				</>
				<cell>boolean: there or not</>
				<cell>Unfolded: PAGE state, never written in a doc (epic pages open folded). A click on the title, a link to it (or into it) and find-in-page set it; set it from code to open it.</>
				<cell/>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Slots" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<text paragraph>Where its children show: a child goes in a slot by its <text code>slot</> attribute.</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>Slot</>
					<cell>What goes in it</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>(default)</>
					<cell>The summary (<text code>&lt;epic-summary&gt;</>), the Kickoff prompt (<text code>&lt;epic-prompt&gt;</>), then the sub-sections (<text code>&lt;epic-section kind="overview-part"&gt;</>s).</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>summary</>
					</>
					<cell>The summary in older docs: <text code>&lt;p slot="summary"&gt;</>; <text code>&lt;epic-summary&gt;</> since P14.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>prompt</>
					</>
					<cell>The prompt in older docs: <text code>&lt;blockquote slot="prompt"&gt;</>, drawn folded; <text code>&lt;epic-prompt&gt;</> since P14, which folds itself.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>actions</>
					</>
					<cell>Buttons of the page's own in its title row (<text code>&lt;ui-button slot="actions"&gt;</>): after the title, before its own buttons; a click on one never folds it. The docs runtime puts the block's bullhorn here too.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Parts" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<text paragraph>Pieces of what it draws, which a page's CSS can style from outside with <text code>::part(name)</>.</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>Part</>
					<cell>What it is</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>base</>
					</>
					<cell>The element's box.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>section</>
					</>
					<cell>The <text code>&lt;ui-section&gt;</> drawing the title bar and fold: its own parts through <text code>::part()</> from inside.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>body</>
					</>
					<cell>Around its children: sets <text code>--epic-stack</> for them.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>note</>
					</>
					<cell>The <text code>Loads from parts/x.html ...</> line, when its part can't load.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>prompt</>
					</>
					<cell>An older doc's folded Kickoff prompt: a <text code>&lt;details&gt;</> around the <text code>prompt</> slot (<text code>&lt;epic-prompt&gt;</> draws its own).</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>estimate</>
					</>
					<cell>The estimate line.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>stage-button</>
					</>
					<cell>"Accept Overview" (an <text code>&lt;epic-stage-button&gt;</>, epic <text code>epic-engine</> I180), last on its title row:  only while the page is reviewed and agrees its Overview.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="States" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<text paragraph>Custom states: CSS can match them with <text code>epic-overview:state(name)</>.</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>State</>
					<cell>When</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>:state(open)</>
					</>
					<cell>Unfolded.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>:state(loaded)</>
					</>
					<cell>Its <text code>source</> part is in.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>:state(error)</>
					</>
					<cell>Its <text code>source</> part couldn't be loaded.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Events" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>Event</>
					<cell>Cancelable</>
					<cell>When</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>ui-opening</>
					</>
					<cell>yes</>
					<cell>About to unfold: its title was clicked. Cancel to stay folded. After the fact for a link.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>ui-closing</>
					</>
					<cell>yes</>
					<cell>About to fold: its title was clicked. Cancel to stay open.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>ui-loaded</>
					</>
					<cell/>
					<cell>The <text code>source</> part arrived and is in its children (as <text code>&lt;ui-section source&gt;</>'s).</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>ui-error</>
					</>
					<cell>yes</>
					<cell>The <text code>source</> part couldn't be loaded; its note says so unless cancelled.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="5. How it looks">
		<icon slot="icon" name="palette"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Its title, <text code>1. Overview</>: folded, one line, its words the tooltip; open, it wraps if it must (2026-10-18).</>
			<item><text bold>Its title bar:</> <text code>1. Overview</> and a lightbulb, on the section band, sticking under the page header while you read inside it.</>
			<item><text bold>The estimate line:</> a clock, <text bold>Estimate:</>, then the total, drawn between the prompt and the sub-sections.</>
			<item><text bold>The sub-sections:</> numbered <text code>1.1</>, <text code>1.2</> ..., each a nested title on the row band. While the page is reviewed, each has review buttons (Make Todo, Revisit: no Approve) and a note box.</>
			<item><text bold>Folding:</> a click on the title folds or unfolds it. On an epic page it starts folded, and the page remembers what you opened. A link into it, or find-in-page, unfolds it.</>
			<item>No colour of its own: the summary and the prompt carry the looks (the prompt on faint violet, your voice: <link target="src-guides-epic-components-colours-html" link="/guides/epic-components/colours.html">the colour scheme</>).</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="6. Written by">
		<icon slot="icon" name="terminal"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item><text code>epic create</>: the template's Overview, with a placeholder summary and one sub-section, <text code>o1</> "Structure".</>
			<item><text code>epic create --prompt "..."</> and <text code>epic prompt &lt;epic&gt; "..."</>: its <text code>&lt;epic-prompt&gt;</>.</>
			<item><text code>estimate</>: rewritten by every command that changes a phase (<text code>epic add-phase</>, <text code>epic update --estimate</> ...): every phase's estimate added up, and what's left. Absent before the first estimated phase.</>
			<item>The summary and the sub-sections' prose: written by hand, by the Claude session planning the epic.</>
			<item><text code>epic update &lt;epic&gt;#o3 underway ...</>: Claude's status cards on a sub-section; a review's Make Todo makes a todo linking it.</>
			<item><text code>epic convert</>: the old Overview, its slotted summary and prompt turned into <text code>&lt;epic-summary&gt;</> and <text code>&lt;epic-prompt&gt;</> by its second pass.</>
		</>
	</>
	<html>
		<footer class="site-page-footer">
			<ui-divider></>
			<ui-text class="meta" paragraph>Last checked 2026-10-09 against branch <ui-text code>epic-components</>: the tables come from its vocabulary file, so they change with it.</>
		</>
	</>
